.TH OURSYNC 1 "2026-11-17" "OurSync" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
oursync \- Google Drive as a filesystem: streamed, with chosen files kept on local disk
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oursync
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B OurSync
presents Google Drive as an ordinary directory tree, by default at
.IR ~/Drive .
Nothing is downloaded until something reads it, so a Drive far larger than the local disk costs
nothing to mount; what has been read is cached and evicted as the cache fills.
.PP
A file that must always be fast, or must survive going offline, is
.IR pinned :
a real copy is placed on local disk, served from there, and never evicted. Pinning is what
.B OurSync
adds to
.BR rclone (1),
whose cache is eviction-based with no way to say
.IR "keep this one" .
.PP
The mount is read-write when the configured Drive remote allows it. Changes made through the mount
reach Drive by themselves. Changes made to Drive elsewhere reach a streamed file within the poll
interval, and a pinned file when
.B oursync refresh
runs.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B pin \fIpath\fR...
Place a real copy of each path on local disk and serve reads from there. A directory is pinned
whole, and afterwards tracks files Drive gains.
.TP
.B unpin \fIpath\fR...
Remove the local copy; the file goes back to streaming. Refuses if the file is not in Drive, so
the only copy cannot be deleted.
.TP
.B refresh \fR[\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fIpath\fR...]
Bring pinned copies back into agreement with Drive. A pin is a cache of Drive, so Drive is the
truth and a pinned file whose Drive copy has changed is re-copied. A local copy that is newer and
differs is a
.I conflict:
it is reported and nothing is overwritten. Exits non-zero if there was a conflict.
.TP
.B list
What is pinned, and what it costs on disk.
.TP
.B status \fIpath\fR...
Whether each path is pinned or streamed.
.TP
.B mount \fR[\fIrclone flags\fR]
Mount Drive, in the foreground. Normally run by
.BR oursync\-mount.service .
Extra arguments are passed to
.BR "rclone mount" .
.TP
.B unmount
Unmount it.
.TP
.B setup \fR[\fB\-\-scope\fR \fIdrive\fR|\fIdrive.readonly\fR]
Create or re-authorise the per-user configuration: the Drive remote, the union over it and the
configuration file. Run once per user after installing, and again with
.B \-\-scope drive
to turn a read-only installation into one that can write. See
.B oursync setup \-\-help
for the rest of its options.
.TP
.B doctor
Print the whole configuration, its current state, and anything wrong with it.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/oursync/oursync.conf
Shell syntax, sourced by
.BR oursync .
Sets the remote and union names, the mount point, the pin directory, the cache directory and its
size and age limits, the write-back delay, an optional bandwidth limit, and the mount's control
port and its generated password.
.TP
.I ~/.config/oursync/pins
What was asked to be kept offline, one per line: a kind
.RB ( d
or
.BR f )
and a path relative to the mount. Distinct from what happens to be on disk, because a pinned
directory must gain the files Drive gains.
.TP
.I ~/.config/oursync/client_secret.json
The OAuth client downloaded from your own Google Cloud project.
.B OurSync
ships no client ID of its own.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/oursync/pinned
The pinned copies. The first upstream of the union, with
.BR :nc ,
so nothing is ever created here by accident.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/oursync
The streaming cache, bounded by
.I CACHE_MAX_SIZE
and
.IR CACHE_MAX_AGE .
.SH SERVICES
.TP
.B oursync\-mount.service
Mounts Drive at login.
.B systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now oursync\-mount.service
.TP
.B oursync\-refresh.timer
Runs
.B oursync refresh \-\-quiet
every five minutes, which is the only thing that keeps a pinned file current when Drive is changed
from somewhere else.
.SH LIMITS
Google's API offers no differential upload, so saving a file uploads all of it however little
changed. Google Docs, Sheets and Slides have no byte stream and appear as stubs. Pin status shows
in Nemo only. One Google account per installation.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The operation failed, or
.B refresh
found a conflict.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was wrong.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rclone (1),
.BR rclone\-mount (1),
.BR fusermount3 (1)
.PP
.UR https://github.com/reckless-technology/oursync
